---
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
const updated = 'October 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Use" description={`Terms of use for the ${site.name} website.`} extraTopPad>
  <div class="container">
    <PageHero kicker="Legal" title="Terms of use" lede={`Reasonable use rules for this website, updated ${updated}.`} />
  </div>

  <article class="section">
    <div class="container-narrow legal">
      <h2>About this site</h2>
      <p>
        This website presents {site.name} — the student Enactus chapter of {site.institution}. It describes our
        projects, publishes our stories and directories, and lets people contact the team. It is not an online
        store with checkout, and no purchases or payments happen through it yet.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        Figures and statements on this site come from chapter-published reports (our earlier site posts and official
        updates), labelled with their sources where relevant. We update as projects report more; if you find an
        error, tell us.
      </p>

      <h2>Using our content</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Our writing, layout code and identity are the chapter's own work.</li>
        <li>
          You're welcome to link to or reference what we publish, with attribution — including photos once they're
          here.
        </li>
        <li>Do not republish our content as your own, fabricate partner relationships using our pages, or scrape product listings.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Enquiries and applications</h2>
      <p>
        Contact and recruitment forms are frontend placeholders — they pass your message to your own email app for
        you to send. Email the chapter directly for anything binding, and expect a human reply from the core team.
      </p>

      <h2>Linking out</h2>
      <p>
        Our Instagram, LinkedIn and Linktree links take you to platforms we don't control; their terms are theirs.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        This site is informational and provided in good faith by a student team. We keep it current and correct it
        when alerted, but can't warranty absolute accuracy at every moment.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="related-pages">
        Also read: <a class="text-link" href="/privacy-policy">Privacy policy</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .legal h2 {
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .legal ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.3rem;
  }

  .legal li::marker {
    color: var(--accent-deep);
  }

  .legal a {
    color: var(--accent-deep);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .related-pages {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
  }
</style>
